.</source><volume>77</volume><year>1981</year><fpage>95</fpage><lpage>117</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6259275</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Heetal1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>He</surname><given-names>D.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Jiang</surname><given-names>J.X.</given-names></name><name><surname>Taffet</surname><given-names>S.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Burt</surname><given-names>J.M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Formation of heteromeric gap junction channels by connexins 40 and 43 in vascular smooth muscle cells</article-title><source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source><volume>96</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>6495</fpage><lpage>6500</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10339616</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Ohetal2000"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oh</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Abrams</surname><given-names>C.K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Verselis</surname><given-names>V.K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bargiello</surname><given-names>T.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stoichiometry of transjunctional voltage&#x02013;gating polarity reversal by a negative charge substitution in the amino terminus of a connexin32 chimera</article-title><source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source><volume>116</volume><year>2000</year><fpage>13</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10871637</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Pauletal1991"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Paul</surname><given-names>D.L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ebihara</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Takemoto</surname><given-names>L.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Swenson</surname><given-names>K.I.</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodenough</surname><given-names>D.A.</given